{
  "note": "Format D held open, on found footage and press photographs. Shots tile continuously. No top mark, no end card. Two layers carry the information the footage cannot: a location tag opens each of the three countries, because a shelter door could be anywhere and the film crosses three in forty seconds; a small flag lands on each country as it is named, because Hawaii, New Zealand and Finland go past in under half a second each and a flag is read before it is looked at; and the Finnish figures are counted up on screen, because fifty thousand and four and a half million are just noises inside a sentence but land as numbers. The tour hosts stay in frame through the middle of the first act — what makes a doomsday condo unsettling is that somebody is showing you round one.",
